{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-3-3","kind":"proposition","title":"垂径定理与逆定理","englishTitle":"If in a circle a straight line through the centre bisect a straight line not through the centre, it also cuts it at right angles; and if it cut it at right angles, it also bisects it.","book":3,"number":3,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.3","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.3/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":3,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":"https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/幾何原本/卷三"}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","contentId":"euclid-3-3","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8f657af3887a5a1bfe7fe4d932795fcaccb6cc79cdf24a1db49d13be8e808cd7","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-3-3.statement","euclid-3-3.construction.1","euclid-3-3.construction.2","euclid-3-3.proof.1","euclid-3-3.proof.2","euclid-3-3.proof.3","euclid-3-3.proof.4","euclid-3-3.proof.5","euclid-3-3.proof.6","euclid-3-3.conclusion","euclid-3-3.historical.1","euclid-3-3.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-3-3.statement","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"9b9986fcce6554a8e6f0a1928267709f9bbb02fba0cc26b775f1fb92b849b9a3","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If in a circle a straight line through the centre bisect a straight line not through the centre, it also cuts it at right angles; and if it cut it at right angles, it also bisects it."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果在圆形中,穿过中心线的直线横穿中心线,那么在直角时,它也会切开;如果在直角时,它也会分割开。"},{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"直线过圜心分他直线为两平分其分处必为两直角为两直角必两平分"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"当一条直线经过圆心时，这条直线会平分圆；在分点处，必有两个直角，而且两个直角必须被平分。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"4be4c9e3277168df033252774b4a759ff45cd466ea72d1c486664f9e6b7f4651","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let ABC be a circle, and in it let a straight line CD through the centre bisect a straight line AB not through the centre at the point F; I say that it also cuts it at right angles."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让ABC圆圈,让一条直线CD通过中心,将一条直线AB通过中心,而不是F点;我说,它也将其剪切为直角。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":2,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d6c3967d7c755fc64cecd3fa7aed7fe57eaadd013d507e59b696eefab83c99f4","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let the centre of the circle ABC be taken, and let it be E; let EA, EB be joined."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"ABC圈的中心部分,E圈;EA圈EB圈。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"dfc3d60af6bbe227860a7d8c0b95652ce9f81b12a42a69fa651968b364c9d409","citations":["euclid-1-8"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Then, since AF is equal to FB, and FE is common, two sides are equal to two sides; and the base EA is equal to the base EB; therefore the angle AFE is equal to the angle BFE. [[I. 8](/principles/euclid-1-8)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"AF等于FB,FE是共同的,两边等于两边;底边 EA等于底边 EB;因此,角度AFE等于角度BFE。 [[I. 8](/principles/euclid-1-8)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b80bbd4bf5c2516c8b4dd2d7cc4cbe7dede89ee66275f0863134c8dfb784f959","citations":["euclid-1-def-10"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But, when a straight line set up on a straight line makes the adjacent angles equal to one another, each of the equal angles is right; [[I. Def. 10](/principles/euclid-1-def-10)] therefore each of the angles AFE, BFE is right."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,当一条直线上设置的直线使相邻角等同于对方时,每一个等角都是对的;因此,每个角AFE,BFE是正确的。 [[I. Def. 10](/principles/euclid-1-def-10)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"2f3bff5c88a77b2789a3258e25f15588006ddeb83876967694e00ee0f1eeff5e","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore CD, which is through the centre, and bisects AB which is not through the centre, also cuts it at right angles."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,通过中心(CD)和不通过中心(AB)的两部分也削减到直角。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6415cb20a080271e36ed4376af023cd5575b4a36655cf59d29fde0e6b16451ff","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Again, let CD cut AB at right angles; I say that it also bisects it. that is, that AF is equal to FB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,CD直角时削减AB;我说,它也是两部分。 也就是说,AF等于FB。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"154fd6eb6d01b443117c03ced0645390caf3f8c94122a3aa782a26eb4ed52f6d","citations":["euclid-1-5"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, with the same construction, since EA is equal to EB, the angle EAF is also equal to the angle EBF. [[I. 5](/principles/euclid-1-5)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由于建造的工程相同,EA等于EB,角度EAF也等于角度EBF。 [[I. 5](/principles/euclid-1-5)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a52c343e839444aa01dff78da2c25ca64b647d77f3942f2464ec49ff2550998c","citations":["euclid-1-26"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the right angle AFE is equal to the right angle BFE, therefore EAF, EBF are two triangles having two angles equal to two angles and one side equal to one side, namely EF, which is common to them, and subtends one of the equal angles; therefore they will also have the remaining sides equal to the remaining sides; [[I. 26](/principles/euclid-1-26)] therefore AF is equal to FB."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,直角 AFE等于直角 BFE,因此,EAF EBF是两个三角形,两个角等于两个角度,一面等于一面,即EF是它们共有的,并分解一个等角;因此,它们也使其余两面等于其余两面;因此,AF等于FB。 [[I. 26](/principles/euclid-1-26)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":9,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d41f4fe56dd428c759377c807a93013dffbbe29c7596acfdac57dd182cad51b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,等等,证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.historical.1","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":10,"kind":"historical_note","title":"徐光启、利玛窦历史中译 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"2d59a751f69d8d022c996d2183ce12c5eacb59e134c44c28747cb332f047572d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"直线过圜心分他直线为两平分其分处必为两直角为两直角必两平分解曰乙丙丁圜有丙戊线过甲心分乙丁线为两平分于己题言甲己必是垂线而己旁为两直角又言己旁既为两直角则甲己分乙丁必两平分先论曰试从甲作甲乙甲丁两线即甲乙己角形之乙己与甲丁己角形之丁己两边等甲己同边甲乙甲丁两线俱从心至界又等即两形等则其对等边之甲己乙甲己丁亦等〈一卷八〉而为两直角矣后论曰如前作甲乙甲丁两线甲乙丁角形之甲乙甲丁两边既等则甲乙丁甲丁乙两角亦等〈一卷五〉又甲乙己角形之甲己乙甲乙己两角与甲丁己角形之甲己丁甲丁己两角各等而对直角之甲乙甲丁两边又等则己乙己丁两边亦等〈一卷廿六〉欲显次论之旨又有一说如甲丁上直角方形与甲己己丁上两直角方形并等〈一卷四七〉而甲乙上直角方形与甲己乙己上两直角方形并亦等即甲己己乙上两直角方形并与甲己己丁上两直角方形并亦等此二率者每减一甲己上直角方形则所存乙己己丁上两直角方形自相等而两边亦等"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"经过圆心的一条直线叫做平分线，在分点处必须有两个直角。这两个直角必须被平分。说明如下：乙丙丁 有一条直线通过 丙戊 和 甲，乙丁 在 己 处被平分。命题说明：甲己 必须是垂直的，己 的一侧是两个直角。此外，由于 己 在两个直角旁边，那么 甲己 必须被平分。乙丁 必须被平分。首先，证明如下：从 甲 出发，从 甲乙甲丁 画两条线，即三角形 丁己 的 甲乙己 和 甲丁己 相等，甲己 在同一侧。两条从中心到边界的线 甲乙甲丁 相等，即两个形状相等。然后对应的 甲己乙甲己丁 也等于 〈一卷八〉，形成两个直角。证明如下：例如，在之前的工作中，两条线 甲乙甲丁 和 甲乙丁 的三角形 甲乙甲丁 的边相等，则 甲乙丁甲丁乙 的两个角也相等。〈一卷五〉 和 甲乙己 的三角形 甲己丁甲丁己 的两个角 甲己乙甲乙己 和 甲丁己 及 甲乙甲丁 的两条边也相等，则 己乙己丁 的两条边相等。〈一卷廿六〉 为说明下一个论点的目的，还有另一个理论：甲丁 和 甲己己丁 上的平方和等于 〈一卷四七〉，甲乙 和 甲己乙己 上的平方也相等，即 甲己己乙 和 甲己己丁 上的两个平方也相等。这两个比相等。对于从 甲己 减去的每一个平方，乙己己丁 上的两个平方相等，且两边相等。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-3.source","contentId":"euclid-3-3","revisionId":"euclid-3-3@raw-8f657af3887a5a1b","order":11,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ae1bf8aff43a7666378dbc4136695c3186bace475d77a3ac6d7960acb6d4cdcb","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.3/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.3\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)\nHistorical Chinese source: https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/幾何原本/卷三"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-3-3:euclid-1-8:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-3-3","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-3-3.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-1-8","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.3","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.3/","sourceLabel":"I. 8"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-3-3:euclid-1-def-10:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-3-3","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-3-3.proof.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-1-def-10","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.3","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.3/","sourceLabel":"I. Def. 10"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-3-3:euclid-1-5:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-3-3","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-3-3.proof.